1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,365
Read a funny A1 story about trying something new.

2
00:00:03,365 --> 00:00:09,723
Follow the story scenes, answer simple questions, and then act the gym role play with a partner.

3
00:00:09,723 --> 00:00:14,958
This is a short school story. Mr. Ping Pong is good at table tennis.

4
00:00:14,958 --> 00:00:18,698
He likes to win, and he talks like a champion.

5
00:00:18,698 --> 00:00:22,812
But one day, the class uses a big jump rope. Mr.

6
00:00:22,812 --> 00:00:27,299
Ping Pong learns that a new thing can be hard at first.

7
00:00:27,299 --> 00:00:28,795
Read each scene first.

8
00:00:28,795 --> 00:00:34,405
When you see the role play, choose two roles and act it with a partner.

9
00:00:34,405 --> 00:00:37,770
Warm-up: What sport or game are you good at?

10
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:42,258
Is it easy to try a new thing in front of people?

11
00:00:42,258 --> 00:00:45,998
What can you say when a friend needs help? Mr.

12
00:00:45,998 --> 00:00:50,859
Ping Pong is famous at school. He is very good at table tennis.

13
00:00:50,859 --> 00:00:56,095
Every day, he carries his racket bag like a champion. He says, "Move, please.

14
00:00:56,095 --> 00:01:01,330
A champion is coming." Some students laugh. Some students think he is rude. Mr.

15
00:01:01,330 --> 00:01:05,818
Ping Pong wants to win every game. When he wins, he smiles.

16
00:01:05,818 --> 00:01:17,411
When he loses, he says, "The floor is bad," or "The ball is strange." He does not like to say, "You played well." On Friday, the class goes to the gym.

17
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:20,403
The teacher has a very long jump rope.

18
00:01:20,403 --> 00:01:24,890
Two students hold the rope and turn it slowly. Whoosh. Whoosh. Whoosh.

19
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:29,378
Some students are excited. Some students are nervous. Mr. Ping Pong laughs.

20
00:01:29,378 --> 00:01:31,248
He says, "This is easy.

21
00:01:31,248 --> 00:01:36,110
It is only a rope." A quiet student named Haru looks at him.

22
00:01:36,110 --> 00:01:41,345
Haru says, "Big jump rope needs timing too." Mr. Ping Pong crosses his arms.

23
00:01:41,345 --> 00:01:46,581
He says, "Timing is my best friend." The teacher smiles and says, "Okay, Mr.

24
00:01:46,581 --> 00:01:51,442
Ping Pong. You can try first." The rope turns. Whoosh. Whoosh. Whoosh. Mr.

25
00:01:51,442 --> 00:01:53,686
Ping Pong stands near the rope.

26
00:01:53,686 --> 00:01:58,922
He wants to jump in, but the rope looks fast. Then he jumps. Smack.

27
00:01:58,922 --> 00:02:03,035
The rope hits his foot and stops. Some students laugh. Mr.

28
00:02:03,035 --> 00:02:04,905
Ping Pong's face is red.

29
00:02:04,905 --> 00:02:08,645
He says, "The rope is too low." He tries again.

30
00:02:08,645 --> 00:02:13,133
This time, he waits too long. The rope hits his back. Smack.

31
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:16,872
Now the gym is quiet. Mr. Ping Pong is angry.

32
00:02:16,872 --> 00:02:19,116
He says, "This rope is stupid.

33
00:02:19,116 --> 00:02:22,482
Table tennis is a real sport." Haru walks closer.

34
00:02:22,482 --> 00:02:27,717
Haru says, "You do not have to be perfect on the first try." Mr.

35
00:02:27,717 --> 00:02:32,205
Ping Pong looks away. He is not angry only at the rope.

36
00:02:32,205 --> 00:02:35,945
He is scared too. He is scared to look weak.

37
00:02:35,945 --> 00:02:40,058
He is scared that people will not think he is special.

38
00:02:40,058 --> 00:02:45,294
The teacher says, "Watch the rope. Listen to the beat." The rope turns again.

39
00:02:45,294 --> 00:02:49,781
Whoosh. Step. Whoosh. Step. Whoosh. Step. Mr. Ping Pong watches. He listens.

40
00:02:49,781 --> 00:02:51,651
The rope is like music.

41
00:02:51,651 --> 00:02:55,391
In table tennis, he also waits for the right time.

42
00:02:55,391 --> 00:02:58,383
Maybe the big rope is not stupid. Mr.

43
00:02:58,383 --> 00:03:03,618
Ping Pong says quietly, "One more try." This time, he does not talk loudly.

44
00:03:03,618 --> 00:03:08,480
He watches the rope. His feet move a little. Haru says, "Now." Mr.

45
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:12,968
Ping Pong steps in. Jump. The rope goes under his feet. Jump.

46
00:03:12,968 --> 00:03:18,203
It goes under his feet again. The students clap and count. "One! Two! Three!

47
00:03:18,203 --> 00:03:21,943
Four!" Then Haru throws a soft table tennis ball. Mr.

48
00:03:21,943 --> 00:03:26,430
Ping Pong jumps and taps the ball back with his racket. Tap.

49
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:30,544
Everyone says, "Wow!" Mr. Ping Pong runs out of the rope.

50
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:35,780
He is tired, but he smiles. He says, "Big jump rope is not stupid.

51
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:41,015
It needs rhythm, timing, practice, and maybe help." Two students act the gym scene.

52
00:03:41,015 --> 00:03:45,877
One student is Haru. One student is Mr. Ping Pong. Read the lines.

53
00:03:45,877 --> 00:03:51,112
Then change one detail. Gym practice: Haru: Are you ready? Mr. Ping Pong: Yes.

54
00:03:51,112 --> 00:03:55,974
I can do this. Haru: Watch the rope. Listen to the beat. Mr.

55
00:03:55,974 --> 00:04:01,210
Ping Pong: It looks fast. Haru: Do not rush. Wait. Mr. Ping Pong: Okay.

56
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:05,697
Tell me when. Haru: Now. Mr. Ping Pong: Jump. I did it!

57
00:04:05,697 --> 00:04:10,185
Haru: Good job. Try two more jumps. Mr. Ping Pong: One. Two.

58
00:04:10,185 --> 00:04:15,420
This is hard, but it is fun. Haru: Do you want the ball too?

59
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:20,282
Mr. Ping Pong: Yes. Throw it softly, please. Haru: Here it comes. Mr.

60
00:04:20,282 --> 00:04:25,518
Ping Pong: Tap. Wow. I can jump and hit. Haru: You have good timing.

61
00:04:25,518 --> 00:04:29,257
Mr. Ping Pong: Thank you. Your help was good too.

62
00:04:29,257 --> 00:04:32,997
QUESTION 1: What sport is Mr. Ping Pong good at?

63
00:04:32,997 --> 00:04:35,989
ANSWER 1: He is good at table tennis.

64
00:04:35,989 --> 00:04:40,102
DISCUSSION 1: What can a good winner say after a game?

65
00:04:40,102 --> 00:04:43,842
QUESTION 2: What does Haru say the big rope needs?

66
00:04:43,842 --> 00:04:46,460
ANSWER 2: Haru says it needs timing.

67
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:50,574
DISCUSSION 2: What new activity is hard for you at first?

68
00:04:50,574 --> 00:04:54,687
QUESTION 3: What happens when Mr. Ping Pong tries two times?

69
00:04:54,687 --> 00:04:59,549
ANSWER 3: The rope hits his foot, and then it hits his back.

70
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:02,914
DISCUSSION 3: What can people say after a mistake?

71
00:05:02,914 --> 00:05:07,402
QUESTION 4: What does the teacher tell Mr. Ping Pong to do?

72
00:05:07,402 --> 00:05:13,012
ANSWER 4: The teacher tells him to watch the rope and listen to the beat.

73
00:05:13,012 --> 00:05:18,247
DISCUSSION 4: Who helps you when you feel nervous? QUESTION 5: What does Mr.

74
00:05:18,247 --> 00:05:19,369
Ping Pong learn?

75
00:05:19,369 --> 00:05:24,605
ANSWER 5: He learns that big jump rope needs rhythm, timing, practice, and help.

76
00:05:24,605 --> 00:05:28,718
DISCUSSION 5: What do you want to practice little by little?

77
00:05:28,718 --> 00:05:32,832
QUESTION 6: What does Haru tell Mr. Ping Pong to do?

78
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:38,442
ANSWER 6: Haru tells him to watch the rope, listen to the beat, and wait.

79
00:05:38,442 --> 00:05:40,685
DISCUSSION 6: Practice the gym scene.

80
00:05:40,685 --> 00:05:44,799
Then change the sport, the number of jumps, or the helper.

81
00:05:44,799 --> 00:05:50,035
Speaking Practice Questions 1. Why does Mr. Ping Pong think the rope is easy?

82
00:05:50,035 --> 00:05:55,270
2. Why is he scared after he misses? 3. How does Haru help him?

83
00:05:55,270 --> 00:06:00,506
4. What is one good sentence to say to a friend after a mistake?

84
00:06:00,506 --> 00:06:04,619
5. Change one scene and act it with a partner. Mr.

85
00:06:04,619 --> 00:06:09,855
Ping Pong is proud, funny, and sometimes difficult. But he can change a little.

86
00:06:09,855 --> 00:06:12,847
At first, he laughs at the big rope.

87
00:06:12,847 --> 00:06:16,212
Then he misses, listens, tries again, and accepts help.

88
00:06:16,212 --> 00:06:23,318
The story teaches a simple lesson: a new thing can feel scary, but practice and help make it easier.

89
00:06:23,318 --> 00:06:27,431
You do not have to be perfect on the first try.
